    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "The concept was written down in late October as a Concept Codex. On 2 November it became a small playable slice in Godot 4.5: the starship as a hub, the crew roster, one banner with its odds and pity shown in the game, and turn-based battles on a speed timeline. It was a throwaway on purpose. The point was to play the idea for the first time instead of reading it, so Nero could pick the battle system, how players get around and the art style.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "By 3 November the design pillars were approved, and building began for real.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
