    }
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "The next prototype had no battles at all. It was about how the game feels in the hand: a Home screen, the Summoning Hall, a full ten-pull with sound made in code (a cutscene for a new 5-star, and a 1-in-10,000 surprise we'll leave you to find), a Crew screen with filters, levels and bonds, and a walkable Bridge furnished with pixel props, where Nero strolls around with lazy yawns and five crew members are there to talk to.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "The story player arrived the same day, with mood busts for every speaker and the first two scripts: the Prologue, *Pull Day*, and *Aria's Double Shift*. Aria hosts the Summoning Hall and also works as the ship's diplomat, and her two jobs are where the story's theme of burnout starts.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
